<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Deliberately empty, and not deletable.

    English needs no plural entries here: every counted phrase in the widget is
    written with `^[…](inflect: true)`, and automatic grammar agreement resolves
    it from the source text. Spanish does not rely on that, so es.lproj has a
    real stringsdict — and a localized resource only ships if the development
    language has its counterpart. Without this file XcodeGen builds no variant
    group, the Spanish plurals are silently left out of the bundle, and the
    widget reads "faltan 1 casillas".

    Adding entries here would *change English*: a value found in this file wins
    over the inflection markup in the key.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
